00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Midnight in Paris is a 2011 fantasy comedy film
written and directed by Woody Allen.

10
00:52:13,333 --> 00:52:19,333
Set in Paris, the film follows Gil Pender (Owen Wilson), a screenwriter and aspiring novelist, who is forced to confront the shortcomings of his relationship with his
materialistic fiancée (Rachel McAdams) and their divergent goals, which become increasingly exaggerated as he travels back in time to the 1920s each night at midnight.

11
00:57:26,666 --> 00:57:32,666
Produced by the Spanish group Mediapro and Allen's US-based Gravier Productions, the film stars Wilson, McAdams, Kathy Bates, Adrien Brody,
Carla Bruni, Tom Hiddleston, Corey Stoll, Alison Pill, Kurt Fuller, Mimi Kennedy, Lea Seydoux, Marion Cotillard, and Michael Sheen.

12
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
It premiered at the 2011 Cannes Film Festival and was
released in the United States on May 20, 2011.

13
01:07:53,333 --> 01:07:59,333
The film opened to critical acclaim.

14
01:13:06,666 --> 01:13:12,666
In 2012, it won the Academy Award for Best Original Screenplay
and the Golden Globe Award for Best Screenplay.

15
01:18:20,000 --> 01:18:26,000
It was nominated for three other Academy Awards: Best
Picture, Best Director and Best Art Direction.

16
01:23:33,333 --> 01:23:39,333
The film explores themes of paris, france, based on novel
or book, detective, screenwriter, camping.

17
01:28:46,666 --> 01:28:52,666
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
